From a15aaa67afa6706db4c8b80ff3463f9c25aa7419 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Himess <semihcvlk53@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:01:45 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] feat(kms-connector): H7 stored-result revalidation and
 persistent H4 attempts (lifecycle Level 1)

Profile H7 (rule V6) in the connector's HTTP endpoint: with
`revalidate_stored_results`, a stored successful user decryption payload is
not served as it is. The endpoint drops it and puts the request back to
`pending`, so the kms-worker runs every check again at a fresh decision
block; duplicates attach to that one revalidation. Public decryption
results are served as stored. The content id already covers the signature
and the validity window (EIP-712 hash of the whole request), so the
endpoint's deduplication meets H7 unchanged.

Profile H4 attempts are kept in the connector database
(`profile_h_erc1271_attempts`, keyed by the request digest), so a worker
restart no longer grants further ERC-1271 attempts.

Tests: three endpoint integration tests (revalidation, duplicates, public
payload) next to Zama's; the kms-worker test setup gets the attempt store.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
